 n of Bram Stoker's classic tale. Towering ominously among the shadows of t
 he Carpathian Mountains\, Castle Dracula strikes fear in the hearts of the
  Transylvanian villagers below. After a naive real estate agent succumbs t
 o the will of Count Dracula\, the two head to London where the vampire hop
 es to stroll among respectable society by day and search for potential vic
 tims by night. Directed by horror specialist Tod Browning\, the film creat
 es an eerie\, chilling mood that has been rarely realized since and remain
